ExecutingRecipe
├── when arithmetic operands are literal
│   ├── it folds checked arithmetic and floor division into uint216 literals
│   ├── it folds the literal limit without narrowing full-width results
│   └── it retains overflow, underflow and division-by-zero failures at runtime
├── when a value was already evaluated
│   ├── it simplifies arithmetic identities without truncating its value
│   ├── it folds multiplication by zero with a positive literal denominator
│   ├── it removes unsigned zero lower bounds for validated inputs and numerical results
│   ├── it reuses identical calculations across actions
│   └── it removes checks already proven true
├── when an operand has not been evaluated
│   ├── it retains missing-input, unknown-source, self-reference and nonnumeric-reference failures
│   └── it ignores unused words, short instructions and conditional bindings as input-validity proofs
├── when a higher input index was evaluated
│   └── it proves lower indices exist, including through a MulDiv denominator
├── when reads or actions occur
│   ├── it retains generic reads even without an intervening action
│   ├── it reuses the same ERC20 balance until any Manage, Approve, Call or ClearApproval instruction
│   ├── it tolerates malformed raw reads during balance lookup without removing them
│   ├── it removes two repeated balance reads from three funding sources
│   ├── it preserves balance caching across ReadIf without caching its optional result
│   ├── it folds validated full-width ReadIf results safely
│   ├── it skips unused adapter reserve queries while consuming the zero-gated runtime
│   ├── it retains action order and runtime indices
│   └── it binds folded operands and reused results in calls and queries
├── when a funding source opts into preparation
│   ├── it calls from the executor before reading capacity even with zero shortfall
│   └── it starts a fresh balance read after preparation
├── when a funding source omits capacity
│   ├── it allows only the final external source with an entirely empty query
│   └── it rejects an absent preparation target with nonempty calldata
├── when an operand carries offset bits ignored by the interpreter
│   └── it returns a canonical operand that can still be packed into a binding
├── when multiplication and division share a factor
│   └── it retains multiplication overflow instead of cancelling the factor
└── when comparing optimized and raw programs
    ├── it preserves all numerical outputs or exact revert data under fuzzing
    ├── it preserves bound full-width reads and fresh state across interleaved calls and managed actions
    ├── it consumes skipped runtime slots and pins distinct active managed recipients
    ├── it matches an independent observation hash and exact token movements from identical snapshots
    ├── it rolls back all prior actions with identical failed-check and overflow revert data
    └── it reduces encoded size and isolated execution gas on a redundant arithmetic fixture
